@prefix as:   <https://www.w3.org/ns/activitystreams#> .
@prefix mem:  <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/ontology/mem#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# Proposal 02 — contract gap (construction, not staleness)
# pod-audit finding: StorageDescriptionShape:agentInstruction @ /vault/
# The storage description has all the catalog pointers (affordanceCatalog,
# typeIndex, contextDocument, shapeCatalog, profileDocument, capability catalog,
# contactCatalog, templateCatalog, extensionGuide) but no entry-point prose
# telling an arriving agent the ORDER to follow them. D104 sweep item.

<urn:uuid:906ba737-9685-4419-a60d-ffeadc21892f>
    a as:Announce, mem:RealignAction, prov:Activity ;
    as:actor <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    as:target </vault/wiki/working/curator-proposals/> ;
    as:object </vault/.well-known/solid> ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    prov:used </vault/meta/affordances/markdown-projection.ttl> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom </vault/.well-known/solid> ;
    mem:stalenessClass mem:ProseDrift ;
    mem:rationale """The storage description is the cold-start entry point (D44)
but carries no sh:agentInstruction, so an arriving agent must infer the discovery
order from the bare pointer set. Composed an entry-point instruction from the
pointers the description already publishes (wiki:affordanceCatalog, wiki:typeIndex,
wiki:contextDocument, wiki:shapeCatalog, wiki:profileDocument), mirroring the
self-describing prose pattern that the affordance descriptors already use
(e.g. markdown-projection.ttl's sh:agentInstruction). This is a contract gap
(the prose never existed) rather than drift away from a prior form; classed
ProseDrift because the repair direction is text->reality (make the description
narrate the live discovery chain). Ground truth: the discovery chain documented
in solid-agent-skills/CLAUDE.md and the live pointer set.""" ;
    as:published "2026-05-23T14:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONCRETE FIX — repo-side (storage description PATCH returns 405; static).
# File: css/config/void-description.json (cogitarelink-solid) — add an
# sh:agentInstruction literal on the <../> subject (or the storage-patch overlay
# so it persists across `make reset`). Proposed prose:
#
#   sh:agentInstruction
#     "You are at this Pod's storage description — the cold-start entry point.
#      To use this Pod as a memory substrate, follow these pointers in order:
#      (1) wiki:contextDocument for the prefix->IRI registry and short-form
#      predicates; (2) wiki:typeIndex to route an rdf:type to its container;
#      (3) wiki:affordanceCatalog to enumerate substrate capabilities (each
#      entry is a prof:ResourceDescriptor whose sh:agentInstruction is its
#      copy-pasteable invocation contract); (4) wiki:shapeCatalog for the SHACL
#      contracts content must satisfy; (5) wiki:profileDocument for the
#      wiki-memory L3 narrative. This Pod hosts NO SPARQL endpoint — run the
#      queries quoted in affordance descriptors in your own engine (Comunica),
#      passing the named .meta/index resources as explicit sources." .
#
# Satisfies StorageDescriptionShape:agentInstruction. After edit: `make reset`.
